From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucas gelfond <lucasgelfond@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 19/29] demux: avi: do not skip data of a track while indexing ahead

When a file has no usable index, Demux_Seekable indexes chunks as it meets
them while looking for data a track needs. Any chunk it met was then made
the current chunk of its track, even when that track was still part way
through an earlier chunk (audio read by bytes) or had earlier chunks left:
the rest of those were silently dropped. With MP3 in an index-less AVI the
packetizer got the start of one chunk followed by the next one and never
found a frame, so the file played without sound.

Only take the chunk when it is the next one its track would read; any other
chunk is just indexed and skipped, and read later from the index.
---
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/modules/demux/avi/avi.c b/modules/demux/avi/avi.c
index 24ec883..73b1302 100644
--- a/modules/demux/avi/avi.c
+++ b/modules/demux/avi/avi.c
@@ -1323,11 +1323,14 @@ static int Demux_Seekable( demux_t *p_demux )
                     index.i_lengthtotal = index.i_length;
                     int64_t i_indexid = avi_index_Append( &tk->idx, &p_sys->i_movi_lastchunk_pos, &index );
 
-                    /* do we will read this data ? */
+                    /* do we will read this data ? Only if it is the next
+                     * chunk of that track: a track that is still inside an
+                     * earlier chunk (or has unread chunks left) must not jump
+                     * ahead, or the rest of its data is lost */
                     if( i_indexid >= 0 &&
+                        tk->i_idxposc == (uint64_t) i_indexid &&
                         AVI_GetDPTS( tk, tk->demuxctx.i_toread ) > -p_sys->i_read_increment )
                     {
-                        tk->i_idxposc = (unsigned int) i_indexid;
                         tk->i_idxposb = 0;
                         break;
                     }
